/* Windows resources for the Strata executable.
 *
 * `assets/branding/windows/strata.ico` is generated by `python3 scripts/generate-icons.py`
 * from `assets/branding/strata-icon.svg`; it carries the 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 128 and 256
 * pixel frames so Explorer, the taskbar, Alt-Tab and the title bar all pick a sharp one.
 *
 * Compile this next to the crate root and pass the result to the linker:
 *
 *   MSVC (Visual Studio command prompt):
 *     rc.exe /fo strata-rc.res windows\strata.rc
 *     set RUSTFLAGS=-C link-arg=strata-rc.res
 *     cargo build --release
 *
 *   MinGW (MSYS2 / UCRT toolchain):
 *     windres windows/strata.rc -O coff -o strata-rc.res
 *     set RUSTFLAGS=-C link-arg=strata-rc.res
 *     cargo build --release
 *
 * Strata does not do this from `build.rs`: a Windows-only build dependency would break the
 * `cargo fetch --offline` step of the offline Flatpak build, so the resource is embedded with
 * the toolchain the Windows build already uses. See `docs/packaging.md`.
 */

1 ICON "assets/branding/windows/strata.ico"